<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Unrolled element copies as memcpy (`option copyrun on|off`, default on;
    stage P3, the late fullloop pass after `repstring`).

    The fixtures are copyrun.c (gcc -O2, x86-64: struct assignments and a
    31-byte memcpy gcc expands into SSE and overlapping 8-byte moves) and the
    i386 repstring fixture, whose 32-byte struct copy gcc -Os expands into
    eight 4-byte moves.

    The first pass of each image (`option copyrun off`) prints one assignment
    per element. The second (the shipped default) prints one builtin_memcpy
    per run: 64 bytes, the same 64 bytes into the second half of one struct,
    the 31 bytes the overlapping moves cover, and the i386 32 bytes. A
    two-word copy keeps its two assignments, and a copy into a frame local
    (`local`) keeps its loads.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
